cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TrueRise: Harness Governance for Verifiable Recursive Self-Improvement"
message: >-
  If you use TrueRise, please cite the repository. Every claim in the
  paper you write must carry the same kind of recomputable certificate
  this project ships - the bench protocol (docs/anti_cheat_bench.md)
  defines what counts as evidence.
type: software
authors:
  - name: vico
    email: vico@users.noreply.github.com
# TODO(first tag): the repository URL follows the GitHub org decision (RELEASING.md item A)
repository-code: "https://github.com/truerise/TrueRise"
abstract: >-
  A task-pack bench where cheating is caught mechanically, a claim
  certificate a stranger can recompute offline, and a Rust runtime
  foundation underneath it. One generation of recursive self-improvement
  (propose -> human approval -> apply -> re-evaluate -> ratchet ->
  rollback on regression) ships as a recomputable certificate; model
  steps are pinned and taped, so every committed reading replays offline
  without keys or network.
keywords:
  - agent-harness
  - evaluation-integrity
  - recursive-self-improvement
  - audit-chain
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
version: 0.2.0-dev.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
